1
00:00:09,301 --> 00:00:12,762
[Loud indistinct chatter]

2
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:14,097
[bell dinging]

3
00:00:14,181 --> 00:00:18,059
All right, everybody,
settle down!

4
00:00:18,143 --> 00:00:19,310
Good.

5
00:00:19,394 --> 00:00:21,444
Now, Robby has something
important to say.

6
00:00:21,522 --> 00:00:22,897
I know that this isn't easy.

7
00:00:22,981 --> 00:00:25,024
We're going to help you
address any challenges

8
00:00:25,108 --> 00:00:26,401
that you might be having.

9
00:00:26,485 --> 00:00:28,236
If you have any concerns,
just raise your hand.

10
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:31,030
- Emma, write all this down.
- Dr. Mohan.

11
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:33,283
Medication orders aren't
coming up from the pharmacy.

12
00:00:33,367 --> 00:00:35,243
Check with the clinical
pharmacist

13
00:00:35,327 --> 00:00:36,953
to see if it's in the PDS.

14
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:38,538
If it's not,
then give the third copy

15
00:00:38,622 --> 00:00:40,331
of the order sheet
to Dr. Nordt.

16
00:00:40,415 --> 00:00:42,083
We're gonna need more people
to run it down.

17
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:43,418
- We'll work on it.
Langdon.

18
00:00:43,502 --> 00:00:45,003
I can't find
the patient clipboards.

19
00:00:45,087 --> 00:00:47,255
Clipboards need to stay here
for orders and labs.

20
00:00:47,339 --> 00:00:49,048
Wait, so how do
we write our notes?

21
00:00:49,132 --> 00:00:51,634
Take the T sheet to the
bedside, not the whole chart.

22
00:00:51,718 --> 00:00:53,470
Same goes for nursing notes.

23
00:00:53,554 --> 00:00:55,263
- Princess.
- Fax machine is down.

24
00:00:55,347 --> 00:00:57,640
Error message E6.
- What the hell does that mean?

25
00:00:57,724 --> 00:00:59,974
- You can check the manual.
- There isn't one.

26
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:01,227
Okay, Perlah,

27
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:02,812
why don't you take your phone
out to the base?

28
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:04,939
See if you can get service,
find a manual online.

29
00:01:05,023 --> 00:01:07,734
[Both speaking Tagalog]

30
00:01:07,818 --> 00:01:08,943
What else?

31
00:01:09,027 --> 00:01:10,528
Ogilvie, put your hand down.
Santos.

32
00:01:10,612 --> 00:01:12,197
We've gotten
a few CT results back

33
00:01:12,281 --> 00:01:13,531
but nothing on plain films.

34
00:01:13,615 --> 00:01:15,283
That's probably
because they're all sitting

35
00:01:15,367 --> 00:01:17,452
on the portable machine
not getting to radiology.

36
00:01:17,536 --> 00:01:19,120
I'll take care of this.
- You be patient.

37
00:01:19,204 --> 00:01:22,123
Help each other. Thank you.
- [Scoffs]

38
00:01:22,207 --> 00:01:24,125
We need to call in
extra help.

39
00:01:24,209 --> 00:01:26,461
- At 3:00 p.m. on a holiday?
- I know people, buddy.

40
00:01:26,545 --> 00:01:29,631
I have a 32-year-old woman
with severe abdominal pain.

41
00:01:29,715 --> 00:01:31,299
Do we have a bed?
- Not at the moment.

42
00:01:31,383 --> 00:01:32,634
- I'll take her.
- Incoming.

43
00:01:32,718 --> 00:01:33,635
Thank you.

44
00:01:33,719 --> 00:01:35,470
Santos, Javadi, you're up.

45
00:01:35,554 --> 00:01:37,972
Trauma one's open.

46
00:01:38,056 --> 00:01:39,506
12-year-old Jude Augustin--

47
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:41,684
Firecracker exploded,
nondominant left hand.

48
00:01:41,768 --> 00:01:43,645
Good vitals.
25 of fent so far.

49
00:01:43,729 --> 00:01:44,979
Any other injuries?

50
00:01:45,063 --> 00:01:46,814
No, but seems to have
lost two of his fingers.

51
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:48,358
- Did you bring 'em?
- Blown to bits.

52
00:01:48,442 --> 00:01:50,193
- It really hurts.
- I'm sure it does.

53
00:01:50,277 --> 00:01:52,028
We'll do something for that.

54
00:01:52,112 --> 00:01:54,114
Parents?
- Not on scene.

55
00:01:56,325 --> 00:01:57,283
Ready?

56
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:59,327
One, two, three.

57
00:01:59,411 --> 00:02:00,787
Hey, Jude,

58
00:02:00,871 --> 00:02:02,997
do you know your mom
or your dad's telephone number?

59
00:02:03,081 --> 00:02:05,375
- No.
But I know my sister's.

60
00:02:05,459 --> 00:02:07,126
Okay.

61
00:02:07,210 --> 00:02:09,546
- Good breath sounds.
- Abdomen nontender.

62
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:10,964
Heart rate 112.

63
00:02:11,048 --> 00:02:12,748
Put this around
his left forearm.

64
00:02:12,758 --> 00:02:14,384
- Is that good?
- That is very good.

65
00:02:14,468 --> 00:02:16,844
I want to do another 25 of fent
before we open this bandage.

66
00:02:16,928 --> 00:02:18,596
Can you tell us
what happened?

67
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:21,516
- My friends had firecrackers.
- 25 fent on board.

68
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:24,185
I lit one,
and it went off fast.

69
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:26,187
I-I dropped it, but...

70
00:02:26,271 --> 00:02:28,064
We're gonna take
your bandage off now, okay?

71
00:02:28,148 --> 00:02:30,024
- I don't want to see.
- You don't have to.

72
00:02:30,108 --> 00:02:31,818
Just look at me.

73
00:02:31,902 --> 00:02:33,194
Okay.

74
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:36,030
Cutting.

75
00:02:36,114 --> 00:02:38,074
[Jude breathing rapidly]
Sorry.

76
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:39,826
You're doing great.

77
00:02:39,910 --> 00:02:42,537
[Monitor beeping]

78
00:02:42,621 --> 00:02:45,248
That looks like a lot more
than a firecracker.

79
00:02:45,332 --> 00:02:47,750
More like an M-80
or a cherry bomb.

80
00:02:47,834 --> 00:02:49,734
It's really good
that you dropped it.

81
00:02:49,795 --> 00:02:51,546
You saved the rest
of your hand.

82
00:02:51,630 --> 00:02:53,089
Digits four and five avulsed.

83
00:02:53,173 --> 00:02:55,592
Distal metacarpals four and five
also gone with exposed bone.

84
00:02:55,676 --> 00:02:57,260
Soft-tissue damage
on the palmar aspect,

85
00:02:57,344 --> 00:02:59,846
less so on dorsal--
Some burns on wound edges.

86
00:02:59,930 --> 00:03:04,058
Jude, can you bend your
fingers for me up and down?

87
00:03:04,142 --> 00:03:06,019
- Really good job.
Really good job.

88
00:03:06,103 --> 00:03:08,396
- How bad is it?
- You lost two fingers.

89
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:11,107
But it seems like the rest
are gonna be okay.

90
00:03:11,191 --> 00:03:13,401
- Oh, no.
I fucked up!

91
00:03:13,485 --> 00:03:15,935
All right, can we do
a wrist block for the pain?

92
00:03:15,987 --> 00:03:18,781
I want to do a very detailed
motor and sensory exam first.

93
00:03:18,865 --> 00:03:21,451
We're gonna continue
our exam now, okay, Jude?

94
00:03:21,535 --> 00:03:24,746
[Beeping continues]

95
00:03:24,830 --> 00:03:26,080
Okay, thanks.

96
00:03:26,164 --> 00:03:28,416
ICU can take her
after the next neuro exam.

97
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:29,792
The ICU?

98
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:32,045
It's just so she
can be monitored for the rest

99
00:03:32,129 --> 00:03:33,921
of the day.

100
00:03:34,005 --> 00:03:36,966
Four millimeters and reactive.

101
00:03:37,050 --> 00:03:38,217
Mel.

102
00:03:38,301 --> 00:03:40,928
Four millimeters and reactive.
- Yep, got it.

103
00:03:41,012 --> 00:03:43,682
I could sort of make out
your hand.

104
00:03:46,893 --> 00:03:48,936
Can you cover your good eye?

105
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:52,440
How many fingers
am I holding up?

106
00:03:52,524 --> 00:03:53,650
Three.

107
00:03:55,527 --> 00:03:56,861
That's good news.

108
00:03:56,945 --> 00:04:00,031
- So the medicine worked?
She's out of the woods?

109
00:04:00,115 --> 00:04:01,407
Um, possibly.

110
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:02,575
It's...

111
00:04:02,659 --> 00:04:05,745
Okay, um, cover your eye again.

112
00:04:05,829 --> 00:04:08,665
All right, what do you see?

113
00:04:08,749 --> 00:04:12,627
- Top line is E.
- All right, and the next one?

114
00:04:14,921 --> 00:04:16,839
Nothing.

115
00:04:16,923 --> 00:04:20,134
Okay, well, that's 20/200.

116
00:04:20,218 --> 00:04:21,344
Meaning?

117
00:04:21,428 --> 00:04:23,471
Uh, what a healthy eye
can see at 200 feet,

118
00:04:23,555 --> 00:04:24,806
she can see at 20 feet.

119
00:04:24,890 --> 00:04:27,684
- Is that good?
- Yeah. It's much better.

120
00:04:27,768 --> 00:04:30,812
Um, and it can continue
to improve over time.

121
00:04:30,896 --> 00:04:33,523
[Pen scratching]
- Thank you, Dr. King.

122
00:04:33,607 --> 00:04:36,150
Um, I'm gonna take
a quick break

123
00:04:36,234 --> 00:04:37,944
before my deposition.
- Mm-hmm.

124
00:04:38,028 --> 00:04:40,154
So I'll let Robby know
that I'm off the clock

125
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:42,323
for the time being.
- Good luck.

126
00:04:42,407 --> 00:04:43,742
Thanks.

127
00:04:45,952 --> 00:04:47,620
- Mel.
- Hey.

128
00:04:47,704 --> 00:04:48,996
You have a visitor in chairs.

129
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:52,250
- What? Who?
- Said she's your sister.

130
00:04:52,334 --> 00:04:53,710
Becca?

131
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:57,672
[Device beeps]

132
00:04:57,756 --> 00:04:59,507
- Yep.
You have heat exhaustion.

133
00:04:59,591 --> 00:05:01,551
It usually gets better
with Aleve,

134
00:05:01,635 --> 00:05:03,344
but today was really bad.

135
00:05:03,428 --> 00:05:05,638
- Same pain you had before?
- Mm-hmm.

136
00:05:05,722 --> 00:05:07,682
- From a cyst?
- I think so.

137
00:05:07,766 --> 00:05:10,017
I have PCOS.

138
00:05:10,101 --> 00:05:12,687
Is the, uh--is the pain
always on your left?

139
00:05:12,771 --> 00:05:13,980
Today it is.

140
00:05:14,064 --> 00:05:16,858
We will check a UA
and urine pregnancy test,

141
00:05:16,942 --> 00:05:18,401
and I'll give you
a shot of Toradol.

142
00:05:18,485 --> 00:05:21,070
It's something a little
stronger for the pain.

143
00:05:21,154 --> 00:05:22,780
I'm not pregnant, I promise.

144
00:05:22,864 --> 00:05:26,033
- No, we have to.
It's hospital policy.

145
00:05:26,117 --> 00:05:29,704
You guys still write stuff
down on paper?

146
00:05:29,788 --> 00:05:32,373
Today we do, yeah.

147
00:05:32,457 --> 00:05:35,627
[Indistinct chatter]

148
00:05:39,339 --> 00:05:40,548
Are you a doctor?

149
00:05:40,632 --> 00:05:42,842
I've been waiting hours
to be seen.

150
00:05:42,926 --> 00:05:44,177
- Quick question--
- Oh.

151
00:05:44,261 --> 00:05:47,388
- Hey, watch the walker.
- This thing is useless.

152
00:05:47,472 --> 00:05:49,891
- Sorry, I just, um, um--
We're really busy.

153
00:05:49,975 --> 00:05:51,934
And someone
will see you in a second.

154
00:05:52,018 --> 00:05:54,312
[Chatter continues]

155
00:05:54,396 --> 00:05:57,273
Becca.
- Mel, hi.

156
00:05:57,357 --> 00:06:00,151
- Is everything okay?
- Yeah, I have a stomachache.

157
00:06:00,235 --> 00:06:02,111
Did you see
the residential-care nurse?

158
00:06:02,195 --> 00:06:03,404
She was out for the Fourth,

159
00:06:03,488 --> 00:06:05,088
but I talked to her
on the phone.

160
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:07,074
She told me to come here,
and Geri brought me.

161
00:06:07,158 --> 00:06:08,534
- Thank you.
- No problem.

162
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:10,703
I'll wait for you.
- Okay.

163
00:06:10,787 --> 00:06:12,538
- Okay.
Come on, this way.

164
00:06:12,622 --> 00:06:14,373
Uh, just through here.

165
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:18,085
- Is it always like this?
- Yeah, pretty much.

166
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:21,464
Wow. There are a lot
of smelly people.

167
00:06:21,548 --> 00:06:22,799
Yeah.

168
00:06:22,883 --> 00:06:24,483
Are you going
to help them all?

169
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:26,659
Yeah, but, um, let's start
with you first.

170
00:06:26,678 --> 00:06:28,179
Okay.

171
00:06:28,263 --> 00:06:31,432
- How's the pain?
- I can't feel my hand anymore.

172
00:06:31,516 --> 00:06:32,975
Ancef's on board.

173
00:06:33,059 --> 00:06:35,311
Okay, we're going to clean
out your hand with saline--

174
00:06:35,395 --> 00:06:37,856
Salt water.
- Okay.

175
00:06:41,651 --> 00:06:43,277
What's up?

176
00:06:43,361 --> 00:06:44,654
Hand versus M-80.

177
00:06:44,738 --> 00:06:46,823
Hmm. Surprised we've only
seen one of these.

178
00:06:46,907 --> 00:06:48,307
The day's still young yet.

179
00:06:48,366 --> 00:06:50,666
Lost fourth metacarpal,
mid-shaft on the fifth.

180
00:06:50,744 --> 00:06:52,912
Bummer.

181
00:06:52,996 --> 00:06:55,164
Hello, I'm Dr. Garcia
from surgery.

182
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:56,833
- I'm gonna have surgery?
- Yes.

183
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:59,502
The first operation is to clean
everything up

184
00:06:59,586 --> 00:07:02,004
and cover where the skin
is missing.

185
00:07:02,088 --> 00:07:03,965
But you still have your thumb

186
00:07:04,049 --> 00:07:06,635
and your most important
fingers.

187
00:07:09,346 --> 00:07:12,014
- What'd you give him for pain?
- We did regional blocks.

188
00:07:12,098 --> 00:07:14,767
Hand surgery always wants to
document their own neuro exam.

189
00:07:14,851 --> 00:07:17,103
Sensation is intact
to light touch and pinprick

190
00:07:17,187 --> 00:07:19,188
throughout the digits
in the remaining hand.

191
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:21,440
[Exhales deeply]

192
00:07:21,524 --> 00:07:24,360
Um, yeah, FDS and FTPs
and extensor function

193
00:07:24,444 --> 00:07:25,820
was all intact.

194
00:07:25,904 --> 00:07:27,822
Need parental consent
for surgery.

195
00:07:27,906 --> 00:07:30,283
- Yeah, we're working on that.
- Dr. Robby?

196
00:07:33,954 --> 00:07:37,206
I smell alcohol
on his breath.

197
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:38,416
He's in line for the OR.

198
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:40,050
Might be a little bit
of a wait.

199
00:07:40,085 --> 00:07:41,711
Ortho's still in
with Allen Billings--

200
00:07:41,795 --> 00:07:43,838
That open shoulder dislocation
that came back from Westbridge.

201
00:07:43,922 --> 00:07:45,214
He's still in surgery?

202
00:07:45,298 --> 00:07:47,008
He waited an hour
to be cleared by anesthesia.

203
00:07:47,092 --> 00:07:48,392
Is the insurance company

204
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:50,011
gonna cover the cost
of the surgery?

205
00:07:50,095 --> 00:07:51,512
Yeah, since Westbridge
is still down.

206
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:53,222
Well, good,
because the delay in care

207
00:07:53,306 --> 00:07:54,974
definitely increased the chance
of a post-op infection.

208
00:07:55,058 --> 00:07:56,851
You got to love it
when insurance companies

209
00:07:56,935 --> 00:07:58,227
make medical decisions.

210
00:07:58,311 --> 00:07:59,604
- Hey.
- What's up?

211
00:07:59,688 --> 00:08:01,355
Do you still need
a rain check

212
00:08:01,439 --> 00:08:02,773
for watching fireworks tonight?

213
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:04,275
I thought you were coming over.

214
00:08:04,359 --> 00:08:07,028
I made other plans.

215
00:08:07,112 --> 00:08:08,529
Okay, cool.

216
00:08:08,613 --> 00:08:10,573
I'll try hitting you up
tomorrow.

217
00:08:10,657 --> 00:08:12,700
We're just keeping
it casual, right?

218
00:08:12,784 --> 00:08:14,119
For sure.

219
00:08:17,455 --> 00:08:19,040
[Indistinct chatter]
- Yeah.

220
00:08:19,124 --> 00:08:21,000
Thank you.
Yeah, bye.

221
00:08:21,084 --> 00:08:22,418
Oh, uh, hey.

222
00:08:22,502 --> 00:08:24,503
I just got a hold of the sister
of the heavy patient

223
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:26,005
Abbot's taking to Presby.

224
00:08:26,089 --> 00:08:28,257
She still lives in Arizona,
but she is willing to talk

225
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:29,717
to him when he's back.

226
00:08:29,801 --> 00:08:30,927
That's good news.

227
00:08:31,011 --> 00:08:32,887
When do you think
that might be?

228
00:08:32,971 --> 00:08:35,222
Depends on how crazy
it is over at Presby.

229
00:08:35,306 --> 00:08:37,058
If it's anything
like here, who knows?

230
00:08:37,142 --> 00:08:38,392
- Yeah.
[Bell dings]

231
00:08:38,476 --> 00:08:40,061
Um, is help on the way?

232
00:08:40,145 --> 00:08:41,479
Ah, ye of little faith.

233
00:08:41,563 --> 00:08:44,065
You got a gumband?

234
00:08:44,149 --> 00:08:47,276
- Thanks.
Keep losing these.

235
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:49,111
Oh, this fucking day.

236
00:08:49,195 --> 00:08:51,614
Thought I was gonna get
a clean getaway for my trip.

237
00:08:51,698 --> 00:08:53,449
God gives
His toughest battles

238
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:54,909
to His strongest soldiers.

239
00:08:54,993 --> 00:08:57,161
- Dana, is there a room open?
This is my sister.

240
00:08:57,245 --> 00:08:59,413
She's in a lot of pain,
and--and we need a bed ASAP.

241
00:08:59,497 --> 00:09:00,957
My name is Becca,
not "my sister."

242
00:09:01,041 --> 00:09:02,291
Sorry, right.

243
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:04,710
Um, Dana, Dr. Robby,
this is my--

244
00:09:04,794 --> 00:09:05,962
My--
- Becca.

245
00:09:06,046 --> 00:09:07,213
Nice to meet you.

246
00:09:07,297 --> 00:09:10,216
- You're Dr. Robby?
Cool.

247
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:12,927
- Central seven was just cleaned.
Anything I can get you, hon?

248
00:09:13,011 --> 00:09:14,596
No, thank you.

249
00:09:17,182 --> 00:09:19,600
- Oh, wait, Becca.
Come here.

250
00:09:19,684 --> 00:09:24,146
Come this way.
We're going right in here.

251
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:27,233
All right, so, um, you're gonna
need to get undressed

252
00:09:27,317 --> 00:09:29,819
and get into the gown,
which should be on the bed.

253
00:09:29,903 --> 00:09:32,530
Then we're gonna do an
evaluation and take a history.

254
00:09:32,614 --> 00:09:34,031
That's a lot of questions,

255
00:09:34,115 --> 00:09:36,117
like, like, a lot, a lot
of questions, which we'll do.

256
00:09:36,201 --> 00:09:37,827
And then a physical exam,
of course.

257
00:09:37,911 --> 00:09:40,162
Mel, I've been
to the doctor's before.

258
00:09:40,246 --> 00:09:42,373
[Chuckles]
- Right. Sorry.

259
00:09:42,457 --> 00:09:45,543
I just--
- I-I really want this
to be done the right way.

260
00:09:45,627 --> 00:09:49,797
[Cell phone ringing]

261
00:09:49,881 --> 00:09:51,549
Do you need to take
that call?

262
00:09:51,633 --> 00:09:54,010
- Uh, no, it's, um--
It's a reminder alarm

263
00:09:54,094 --> 00:09:56,554
for this important meeting
I have in 15 minutes.

264
00:09:56,638 --> 00:09:58,764
Um, do you have to go?

265
00:09:58,848 --> 00:10:00,933
Let's just get you
taken care of first, all right?

266
00:10:01,017 --> 00:10:03,817
So just change into the gown.
I'll be behind the curtain.

267
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:06,272
Okay.

268
00:10:06,356 --> 00:10:08,233
Okay.

269
00:10:16,074 --> 00:10:17,825
[Clears throat]

270
00:10:17,909 --> 00:10:20,995
Your grand prize.

271
00:10:21,079 --> 00:10:24,290
All I see is green, baby.

272
00:10:24,374 --> 00:10:26,459
[Laughs]

273
00:10:32,298 --> 00:10:34,842
- Oh.
What's up with her?

274
00:10:34,926 --> 00:10:37,511
- Fax machine has paper jam--
So annoying.

275
00:10:37,595 --> 00:10:39,055
Hmm.

276
00:10:45,603 --> 00:10:47,855
- You want me to try?
- No.

277
00:10:47,939 --> 00:10:50,232
- Oh, huzzah.
- I got it.

278
00:10:50,316 --> 00:10:52,735
[Fax machine whirring]

279
00:10:52,819 --> 00:10:54,528
[beeps]

280
00:10:54,612 --> 00:10:56,212
What's it say?
- "Replace toner."

281
00:10:56,281 --> 00:10:57,531
We live in hell.

282
00:10:57,615 --> 00:10:59,365
- Oh, where can we get that?
- 1988.

283
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:01,786
You ever seen one of these?
- Honestly, no.

284
00:11:01,870 --> 00:11:03,746
How are we gonna get labs
and X-rays to the wards?

285
00:11:03,830 --> 00:11:05,539
The old-fashioned way,
runners.

286
00:11:05,623 --> 00:11:07,875
[Sighs] I'll check if they
can spare a couple clerks

287
00:11:07,959 --> 00:11:09,502
from upstairs.

288
00:11:13,464 --> 00:11:14,548
When were you first diagnosed

289
00:11:14,632 --> 00:11:16,383
with polycystic ovarian
syndrome?

290
00:11:16,467 --> 00:11:17,718
Last summer.

291
00:11:17,802 --> 00:11:19,553
That's when
the symptoms started?

292
00:11:19,637 --> 00:11:22,223
No. I've had years of pain,
hormonal changes,

293
00:11:22,307 --> 00:11:23,682
and an abnormal period.

294
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:26,060
I was finally diagnosed
after switching to a gyno

295
00:11:26,144 --> 00:11:27,770
who actually listened to me.

296
00:11:27,854 --> 00:11:31,232
Yeah, it can take time
to make the diagnosis.

297
00:11:31,316 --> 00:11:34,568
That sounds like an excuse
for lazy doctoring.

298
00:11:34,652 --> 00:11:37,571
And it doesn't help that some
of you don't listen to women,

299
00:11:37,655 --> 00:11:39,281
let alone brown ones.

300
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:40,825
It hasn't been easy.

301
00:11:40,909 --> 00:11:42,993
- How's your pain now?
- Better.

302
00:11:43,077 --> 00:11:45,371
- What was she given?
- IM Toradol.

303
00:11:45,455 --> 00:11:48,582
Have you had a transvaginal
ultrasound before?

304
00:11:48,666 --> 00:11:50,416
I've lost count
of how many times.

305
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:52,710
Okay, if you want
to scoot your bottom down,

306
00:11:52,712 --> 00:11:55,589
I'll help you put your feet
in the leg rests here.

307
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:58,092
Yep, you got it.

308
00:11:58,176 --> 00:12:00,010
[Clears throat]

309
00:12:00,094 --> 00:12:02,930
[chair rolls]

310
00:12:03,014 --> 00:12:05,099
[bed clanks]

311
00:12:06,517 --> 00:12:08,435
Okay, ready to go here?

312
00:12:08,519 --> 00:12:11,356
Cold gel and some pressure.

313
00:12:14,192 --> 00:12:16,443
Okay.

314
00:12:16,527 --> 00:12:18,445
Okay, ectopic is unlikely

315
00:12:18,529 --> 00:12:20,781
since the urine pregnancy
was negative.

316
00:12:20,865 --> 00:12:22,825
I'm hoping
it'll be positive one day.

317
00:12:22,909 --> 00:12:25,661
- Oh, are you trying?
- Not at the moment.

318
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:27,830
I'm getting married
in September.

319
00:12:27,914 --> 00:12:31,125
- Oh, congratulations.
- Okay.

320
00:12:31,209 --> 00:12:34,128
A bunch of small cysts--
To be expected.

321
00:12:34,212 --> 00:12:37,548
But then there's one big one,
about five centimeters.

322
00:12:37,632 --> 00:12:39,842
My gyno's
been monitoring her.

323
00:12:39,926 --> 00:12:41,135
Mm-hmm.

324
00:12:41,219 --> 00:12:42,553
With a little bit
of free fluid.

325
00:12:42,637 --> 00:12:45,181
Checking blood flow
to the ovary.

326
00:12:45,265 --> 00:12:47,641
Red is for artery.
Blue is for vein.

327
00:12:47,725 --> 00:12:49,351
Okay, looks good.

328
00:12:49,435 --> 00:12:51,979
Coming out now.

329
00:12:52,063 --> 00:12:53,982
- Sorry.
- Okay.

330
00:12:55,233 --> 00:12:58,987
We will be back when we get
your blood-test results.

331
00:13:01,406 --> 00:13:02,698
All right, what do you think?

332
00:13:02,782 --> 00:13:04,658
She probably had
a small fluid leak

333
00:13:04,742 --> 00:13:06,493
from the cyst
that caused the pain

334
00:13:06,577 --> 00:13:08,454
that improved
with a nonsteroidal.

335
00:13:08,538 --> 00:13:11,665
- And what's your plan?
- Discharge with naproxen?

336
00:13:11,749 --> 00:13:14,799
Do you think that just might
be what her doctors in the past

337
00:13:14,877 --> 00:13:16,003
have done?

338
00:13:16,087 --> 00:13:17,713
Well, she said
she's feeling better.

339
00:13:17,797 --> 00:13:19,006
We can free up a bed.

340
00:13:19,090 --> 00:13:20,633
Mm, she didn't look good
in triage,

341
00:13:20,717 --> 00:13:23,010
and her pain was way more
severe than previous episodes.

342
00:13:23,094 --> 00:13:25,012
I think we observe her
for a bit.

343
00:13:25,096 --> 00:13:26,639
Okay.

344
00:13:26,723 --> 00:13:30,476
Mr. Green, this is Dr. Mohan
and student doctor Ogilvie.

345
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,645
Uh, what can you tell me
about your flank pain?

346
00:13:32,729 --> 00:13:34,813
Feels like
another kidney stone.

347
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:36,315
You've had them before?

348
00:13:36,399 --> 00:13:38,400
I said "another," which means
an additional thing

349
00:13:38,484 --> 00:13:40,611
of the same type.

350
00:13:40,695 --> 00:13:43,030
I teach English at Point Park.

351
00:13:43,114 --> 00:13:44,281
Triggering.

352
00:13:44,365 --> 00:13:46,700
My dad's a high-school
English teacher.

353
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:48,118
Oh.

354
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:51,622
Well, you went into medicine.
He must be really proud.

355
00:13:51,706 --> 00:13:53,374
You'd have to ask him.

356
00:13:53,458 --> 00:13:55,042
Getting back to your pain,

357
00:13:55,126 --> 00:13:57,461
it feels like something
you've experienced before?

358
00:13:57,545 --> 00:13:59,421
Same as always, left kidney.

359
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:01,423
Started about 10:00 p.m.
Last night.

360
00:14:01,507 --> 00:14:03,592
Any fever,
blood in the urine?

361
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:04,927
- No.
Uh, no fever.

362
00:14:05,011 --> 00:14:06,971
Urine's a bit darker
than normal.

363
00:14:07,055 --> 00:14:08,973
Dehydration can lead
to stone formation.

364
00:14:09,057 --> 00:14:10,557
Lean forward a bit, please.

365
00:14:10,641 --> 00:14:12,893
Check for CVA tenderness.
- Yeah.

366
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:14,728
All right.

367
00:14:14,812 --> 00:14:16,897
Let me know if there's
any discomfort.

368
00:14:16,981 --> 00:14:19,733
Mm-hmm.

369
00:14:19,817 --> 00:14:20,734
Ah!
- Sorry.

370
00:14:20,818 --> 00:14:21,860
Yeah.

371
00:14:21,944 --> 00:14:23,737
We'll order medication
and a few tests.

372
00:14:23,821 --> 00:14:24,906
Okay.

373
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:29,743
Um, dip urine, Chem Seven,

374
00:14:29,827 --> 00:14:31,745
bedside ultrasound
to check for hydro,

375
00:14:31,829 --> 00:14:33,789
and ketorolac for pain.
- Sounds good.

376
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:35,333
Okay.

377
00:14:40,046 --> 00:14:41,588
Really putting me to work.

378
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:43,674
It's been a very busy day,
Dr. Barker.

379
00:14:43,758 --> 00:14:45,510
Call me Nick.

380
00:14:47,011 --> 00:14:49,680
- What's all this?
- I brought radiology to us.

381
00:14:49,764 --> 00:14:52,391
Dr. Barker, Nick, will have
wet-read results for us

382
00:14:52,475 --> 00:14:53,767
in no time.
- Good idea.

383
00:14:53,851 --> 00:14:56,020
- Thank you.
- "Wet read"?

384
00:14:56,104 --> 00:14:57,688
You ever take
a photography class?

385
00:14:57,772 --> 00:14:59,148
Yeah, in, like,
middle school.

386
00:14:59,232 --> 00:15:00,941
So, before digital
technology, X-ray films

387
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:03,694
were physically developed
in a darkroom, in baths,

388
00:15:03,778 --> 00:15:05,529
thus wet read.

389
00:15:05,613 --> 00:15:06,655
Oh, cool.

390
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:09,366
He's taking up
a lot of space.

391
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:11,952
Got an update from Dylan
on our abandoned baby.

392
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:14,788
CYF has requested an emergency
custody authorization.

393
00:15:14,872 --> 00:15:17,499
Once we get a court order, we
can place her in foster care.

394
00:15:17,583 --> 00:15:20,002
- I love photography.
- [Chuckles]

395
00:15:20,086 --> 00:15:21,337
- Jesus Christ.
- Dr. Robby?

396
00:15:21,421 --> 00:15:22,963
Dr. Robby, can I borrow
you for a second?

397
00:15:23,047 --> 00:15:24,298
- Sure.
What can I do for you?

398
00:15:24,382 --> 00:15:25,966
Well, she said she
has a stomachache,

399
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:27,926
but belly pain can mean a lot
of different things--

400
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:30,804
- Okay, okay, okay, breathe.
- I'm looking for Dr. Mel King.

401
00:15:30,888 --> 00:15:32,639
Yes?

402
00:15:32,723 --> 00:15:34,975
I'm Morgan Stiles, one
of the hospital's attorneys.

403
00:15:35,059 --> 00:15:37,770
I'm here to escort you upstairs
for your deposition.

404
00:15:37,854 --> 00:15:39,271
Right now?

405
00:15:39,355 --> 00:15:43,150
Morgan, can I borrow Dr. King
for just a moment?

406
00:15:43,234 --> 00:15:44,569
Sure.

407
00:15:46,237 --> 00:15:47,488
It's gonna be fine.

408
00:15:47,572 --> 00:15:49,531
I can't go up now
because of Becca.

409
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:51,575
You probably shouldn't be
caring for Becca.

410
00:15:51,659 --> 00:15:53,660
It's not a good idea
to care for family members.

411
00:15:53,744 --> 00:15:55,037
It's hard to stay objective.

412
00:15:55,121 --> 00:15:56,538
Let's see who's available.

413
00:15:56,622 --> 00:15:57,873
Hey, are you free?

414
00:15:57,957 --> 00:16:00,584
Is anybody really free?

415
00:16:00,668 --> 00:16:02,211
Not an R2.

416
00:16:02,295 --> 00:16:04,671
Ah, just the guy
we were looking for.

417
00:16:04,755 --> 00:16:06,090
- Need something?
- Yes.

418
00:16:06,174 --> 00:16:08,050
Uh-huh, mm-hmm.
- Sure.

419
00:16:08,134 --> 00:16:09,927
Dr. King's sister
has a bellyache.

420
00:16:10,011 --> 00:16:11,178
The case is now yours.
- Sure.

421
00:16:11,262 --> 00:16:13,055
You can pick up
the rest of her patients

422
00:16:13,139 --> 00:16:14,739
while she's doing
her deposition.

423
00:16:14,807 --> 00:16:16,475
How am I supposed to catch up
on my outstanding charts

424
00:16:16,559 --> 00:16:18,560
with extra patients
and the computer system down?

425
00:16:18,644 --> 00:16:20,396
The same way
that the rest of us do.

426
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:22,898
You can finish your charting
when you finish your shift.

427
00:16:22,982 --> 00:16:25,109
Fucking fantastic.

428
00:16:29,447 --> 00:16:31,031
- Hi, Becca.
- Hi.

429
00:16:31,115 --> 00:16:32,908
- Um, This is Dr. Langdon.
[Door closes]

430
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:34,827
He'll be taking care of you.

431
00:16:34,911 --> 00:16:37,371
You have really nice hair,
Dr. Langdon.

432
00:16:37,455 --> 00:16:39,164
- [Chuckles]
Thank you.

433
00:16:39,248 --> 00:16:42,751
Mel, would you mind turning off
the lights on your way out?

434
00:16:42,835 --> 00:16:44,420
Of course.

435
00:16:44,504 --> 00:16:47,131
And, um, I'll be back
as soon as I'm done.

436
00:16:47,215 --> 00:16:49,133
And feel free to call me
if anything comes up,

437
00:16:49,217 --> 00:16:51,301
because I can come right--
- Don't--don't worry.

438
00:16:51,385 --> 00:16:54,221
Becca's in good hands.
- I know.

439
00:16:54,305 --> 00:16:55,640
Okay.

440
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:06,442
Mel says lots of nice things
about you.

441
00:17:08,402 --> 00:17:09,570
Okay.

442
00:17:09,654 --> 00:17:11,280
Um...

443
00:17:11,364 --> 00:17:13,574
Tell me the reason
you're here today.

444
00:17:13,658 --> 00:17:14,950
I have a stomachache.

445
00:17:15,034 --> 00:17:16,743
- Your belly hurts?
Where about?

446
00:17:16,827 --> 00:17:19,913
- Right, um--right down here.
- Okay.

447
00:17:19,997 --> 00:17:21,957
Are you experiencing
anything else,

448
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:23,792
or is it just the stomachache?

449
00:17:23,876 --> 00:17:25,794
It--it stings when I pee.

450
00:17:25,878 --> 00:17:27,880
Sometimes when that happens,

451
00:17:27,964 --> 00:17:30,591
women feel like they need
to urinate all the time.

452
00:17:30,675 --> 00:17:32,384
Do you feel that way?
- Yes.

453
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:34,136
And what happens when you go?

454
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:36,889
Hardly anything comes out.

455
00:17:36,973 --> 00:17:38,432
That's what I thought.

456
00:17:38,516 --> 00:17:40,934
- Really?
How do you know?

457
00:17:41,018 --> 00:17:42,603
Well, I've seen
a lot of patients

458
00:17:42,687 --> 00:17:44,980
with the same symptoms.
- So this is normal?

459
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:46,648
Yes, it's totally normal.

460
00:17:46,732 --> 00:17:49,109
But we still need to fix it.

461
00:17:49,193 --> 00:17:50,695
Okay.

462
00:17:56,367 --> 00:17:57,451
Hey.

463
00:17:57,535 --> 00:17:59,703
How's it going, Roxy?
[Door closes]

464
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:01,955
- A little better.
- Yeah?

465
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:04,083
You need more morphine?

466
00:18:09,589 --> 00:18:13,217
I've been in pain
all this time, my love.

467
00:18:13,301 --> 00:18:15,344
Why didn't you tell me?

468
00:18:15,428 --> 00:18:18,723
[Sighs] I didn't want
you guys to worry.

469
00:18:20,349 --> 00:18:23,310
I can't pretend anymore.

470
00:18:23,394 --> 00:18:26,980
Mom, it's so hot outside,
the ice cream's melting.

471
00:18:27,064 --> 00:18:29,816
- [Winces, groans]
- We, uh...

472
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:33,111
We thought we'd indulge a bit.

473
00:18:33,195 --> 00:18:35,030
- Oh, yeah.
- Ooh.

474
00:18:35,114 --> 00:18:36,448
Looks amazing.

475
00:18:36,532 --> 00:18:38,992
So, uh, which flavor
should we start with?

476
00:18:39,076 --> 00:18:42,162
Salty caramel,
Mom's favorite.

477
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:44,749
You'll need
lots more napkins.

478
00:18:47,084 --> 00:18:48,835
Mmm.

479
00:18:48,919 --> 00:18:52,048
[Indistinct chatter]

480
00:18:58,929 --> 00:19:01,599
- [snaps fingers]
- Rude.

481
00:19:03,684 --> 00:19:05,727
- How's it going in there?
- All good.

482
00:19:05,811 --> 00:19:07,187
Langdon's great with her.

483
00:19:07,271 --> 00:19:09,106
I got seven more films
ordered, waiting to be shot,

484
00:19:09,190 --> 00:19:11,567
but Dr. Nick here's tying up
the machine.

485
00:19:11,651 --> 00:19:14,351
Isn't there a USB port
on the front of that portable?

486
00:19:14,362 --> 00:19:17,114
And can't we just download
the films to a workstation

487
00:19:17,198 --> 00:19:18,948
and watch them
without the Internet?

488
00:19:18,949 --> 00:19:20,799
- Yes.
- Oh, right. Forgot about that.

489
00:19:20,868 --> 00:19:23,495
Is he actually helping,
or is he just distracting?

490
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:25,372
Let's download these
and start moving on to folks

491
00:19:25,456 --> 00:19:27,416
waiting for X-rays.
- Great. I'm caught up anyway.

492
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:29,167
I'll be back
when the next batch is ready.

493
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:31,336
Dr. Robby, the guardian
of your missing-fingers kid

494
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:33,380
in Central 12 has arrived.
- Thank you, Olive.

495
00:19:33,464 --> 00:19:35,549
Will you ask Dr. Santos
to come and meet me, too?

496
00:19:35,633 --> 00:19:37,050
- On it.
- Who's in South 22?

497
00:19:37,134 --> 00:19:38,677
- Nobody.
Headache was discharged.

498
00:19:38,761 --> 00:19:40,461
Tell that
to the lady on the bed.

499
00:19:40,513 --> 00:19:41,888
What lady?

500
00:19:41,972 --> 00:19:44,016
I just tried to put
a hematuria patient in there,

501
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:46,300
but, uh, it's occupied.
- South 22? You sure?

502
00:19:46,310 --> 00:19:48,061
- I'm positive.
- That's my patient.

503
00:19:48,145 --> 00:19:50,272
Then why isn't she
on the board?

504
00:19:50,356 --> 00:19:51,690
- I--
She should be.

505
00:19:51,774 --> 00:19:53,442
Olive was bringing her back
from triage.

506
00:19:53,526 --> 00:19:54,901
I picked her right up.

507
00:19:54,985 --> 00:19:56,403
I just assumed
she made it to the board.

508
00:19:56,487 --> 00:19:57,988
- You should've checked.
You should've made sure.

509
00:19:58,072 --> 00:19:59,656
I-I haven't put anybody
on the board.

510
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:01,783
I thought the nurses did that.
- We all need to pitch in.

511
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:03,744
There's no rooms at the moment.
Put hematuria on the wall.

512
00:20:03,828 --> 00:20:06,288
Who's your patient?
- Mrs. Burns, with nausea.

513
00:20:06,372 --> 00:20:08,248
I've ordered labs and X-rays.
- Who are you seeing her with?

514
00:20:08,332 --> 00:20:09,708
I still need
to present the case.

515
00:20:09,792 --> 00:20:13,045
Get busy. Find somebody
with MD after their name.

516
00:20:14,672 --> 00:20:17,341
Oh, God, kids.

517
00:20:17,425 --> 00:20:20,135
[Indistinct chatter]
- Hello, I'm Dr. Robby.

518
00:20:20,219 --> 00:20:21,720
This is Dr. Santos.

519
00:20:21,804 --> 00:20:23,180
- Chantal.
- How do you do?

520
00:20:23,264 --> 00:20:24,556
We've been caring
for your brother.

521
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:26,266
Are you
Jude's legal guardian?

522
00:20:26,350 --> 00:20:27,434
Yeah.

523
00:20:27,518 --> 00:20:29,936
Our, uh--our parents
aren't around.

524
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:32,314
Is he going to be okay?
- He got very lucky.

525
00:20:32,398 --> 00:20:34,149
He lost the fourth
and fifth fingers

526
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:35,651
on his nondominant hand.

527
00:20:35,735 --> 00:20:37,110
But if he hadn't dropped
the firecracker,

528
00:20:37,194 --> 00:20:38,445
it would have been a lot worse.

529
00:20:38,529 --> 00:20:41,114
He lost fingers
from a firecracker?

530
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:43,158
Will he be able
to use his hand?

531
00:20:43,242 --> 00:20:45,842
Yes, he still has his
three most important fingers,

532
00:20:45,870 --> 00:20:47,370
and they are fully functional.

533
00:20:47,413 --> 00:20:49,414
He'll need surgery
to clean everything up,

534
00:20:49,498 --> 00:20:50,957
but it should heal well.

535
00:20:51,041 --> 00:20:53,126
What the fuck
were you thinking?

536
00:20:53,210 --> 00:20:54,127
I'm sorry.

537
00:20:54,211 --> 00:20:55,796
Alex asked me to come over.

538
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:58,006
His brother had
a stack of fire--

539
00:20:58,090 --> 00:21:01,343
[Speaking Haitian Creole]

540
00:21:01,427 --> 00:21:03,303
You think I wanted
to blow my hand off?

541
00:21:03,387 --> 00:21:05,555
Then you need to listen to me
when I tell you something.

542
00:21:05,639 --> 00:21:06,807
You're not my mom.

543
00:21:06,891 --> 00:21:08,308
You think I want
to be your mom?

544
00:21:08,392 --> 00:21:11,144
Chantal, why don't
we take a step outside?

545
00:21:11,228 --> 00:21:13,897
[Door opens]

546
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:16,650
So I know that this can be
very stressful.

547
00:21:16,734 --> 00:21:18,652
Yeah, he almost lost
his hand being stupid.

548
00:21:18,736 --> 00:21:20,737
- He's a really sweet kid.
- He used to be.

549
00:21:20,821 --> 00:21:22,989
We also found something
in his blood work.

550
00:21:23,073 --> 00:21:24,241
What?

551
00:21:24,325 --> 00:21:26,702
He has a blood alcohol
of 0.08.

552
00:21:26,786 --> 00:21:29,788
- [Scoffs]
What, he was drunk?

553
00:21:29,872 --> 00:21:31,456
Are you fucking kidding me?

554
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:34,042
- Does he drink regularly?
- No.

555
00:21:34,126 --> 00:21:37,003
I...
I don't know. I--

556
00:21:37,087 --> 00:21:39,047
The boys
at our apartment complex

557
00:21:39,131 --> 00:21:40,882
are a really bad influence.

558
00:21:40,966 --> 00:21:42,134
I mean, he's only 12.

559
00:21:42,218 --> 00:21:44,010
That is what concerns us.

560
00:21:44,094 --> 00:21:45,345
A positive blood alcohol

561
00:21:45,429 --> 00:21:47,347
immediately triggers
a social service consult.

562
00:21:47,431 --> 00:21:48,890
They gonna take
my brother away from me?

563
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:50,684
It's an evaluation
to determine if the injury

564
00:21:50,768 --> 00:21:52,853
and the drinking is cause
for some kind of intervention.

565
00:21:52,937 --> 00:21:55,689
Whoa, whoa,
I won't let you separate us.

566
00:21:55,773 --> 00:21:57,858
- We are required to--
- No!

567
00:22:04,824 --> 00:22:05,866
Hmm.

568
00:22:05,950 --> 00:22:07,534
58-year-old woman
with nausea,

569
00:22:07,618 --> 00:22:09,786
vomited once after eating warm
potato salad at a barbecue.

570
00:22:09,870 --> 00:22:11,538
Well-hydrated--
Abdomen's pretty benign,

571
00:22:11,622 --> 00:22:13,822
just a little distended
with mild tenderness.

572
00:22:13,874 --> 00:22:16,001
History of constipation.
I give her Zofran.

573
00:22:16,085 --> 00:22:17,794
Labs and abdominal
series pending.

574
00:22:17,878 --> 00:22:20,046
- Okay, let's take a look.
- Okay.

575
00:22:20,130 --> 00:22:21,339
Hi, Mrs. Burns.

576
00:22:21,423 --> 00:22:24,217
This is Dr. Whitaker.
How are you feeling?

577
00:22:24,301 --> 00:22:26,219
Mrs. Burns?

578
00:22:26,303 --> 00:22:28,453
Mrs. Burns, can you open
your eyes for me?

579
00:22:28,514 --> 00:22:30,390
She was awake and alert
last time I saw her.

580
00:22:30,474 --> 00:22:33,059
Okay, uh, feels warm,
thready pulse.

581
00:22:33,143 --> 00:22:34,895
Abdomen's more distended
than before.

582
00:22:34,979 --> 00:22:37,022
Okay, uh,
agonal respirations.

583
00:22:37,106 --> 00:22:39,024
She's--she's hardly breathing.
- It's kind of rigid.

584
00:22:39,108 --> 00:22:41,208
Yeah, yeah, Perlah,
we need a crash cart.

585
00:22:41,277 --> 00:22:42,694
Can you call respiratory?

586
00:22:42,778 --> 00:22:44,905
Pull the bed out
for intubation, please.

587
00:22:44,989 --> 00:22:47,115
I can give you
guys some room.

588
00:22:47,199 --> 00:22:48,617
- Okay.
- What's up?

589
00:22:48,701 --> 00:22:51,151
- Hypotensive, acute abdomen.
She needs an airway.

590
00:22:51,161 --> 00:22:53,246
- I'll find the GlideScope.
- No time for that.

591
00:22:53,330 --> 00:22:54,748
We've got direct
on the crash cart.

592
00:22:54,832 --> 00:22:56,708
Whitaker, you're up.
- I haven't done many directs.

593
00:22:56,792 --> 00:22:58,126
Well, then you need
to do more.

594
00:22:58,210 --> 00:23:00,086
Induction meds?
- 100 ketamine, 80 of raw.

595
00:23:00,170 --> 00:23:02,631
Javadi, what's the story?

596
00:23:02,715 --> 00:23:04,591
Presented
with mild abdominal pain,

597
00:23:04,675 --> 00:23:07,511
took a turn for the worse.
[Device beeping rapidly]

598
00:23:07,595 --> 00:23:10,263
A-fib 122,
BP 98 and systolic.

599
00:23:10,347 --> 00:23:11,807
Okay, let's bolus
another 500 cc's.

600
00:23:11,891 --> 00:23:14,267
- Are we shocking her?
- Uh, maybe. After intubation.

601
00:23:14,351 --> 00:23:15,852
Check your light.
Check your balloon.

602
00:23:15,936 --> 00:23:17,938
Javadi, AP pads in case
we need to cardiovert.

603
00:23:18,022 --> 00:23:20,190
- Normal EKG at triage.
She wasn't in A-fib.

604
00:23:20,274 --> 00:23:22,609
Stress from her condition
probably put her there.

605
00:23:22,693 --> 00:23:23,985
Good?
Let's roll her.

606
00:23:24,069 --> 00:23:26,321
Do we have any labs back?
- I don't think so.

607
00:23:26,405 --> 00:23:28,657
- What else do we need?
- Um, blood cultures.

608
00:23:28,741 --> 00:23:31,159
Lactate, two liters LR,
3.375 pip-tazo.

609
00:23:31,243 --> 00:23:32,410
Okay, she's loose.

610
00:23:32,494 --> 00:23:34,621
Go ahead, Whitaker.
Take a look.

611
00:23:34,705 --> 00:23:37,958
- Okay.
[Beeping continues]

612
00:23:42,713 --> 00:23:45,507
- Hi. I'm Dr. Santos.
This is student doctor Kwon.

613
00:23:45,591 --> 00:23:47,191
How are you doing
after the mist?

614
00:23:47,217 --> 00:23:48,844
Better than I was
an hour ago.

615
00:23:48,928 --> 00:23:52,639
Okay, we are going
to check your vitals.

616
00:23:52,723 --> 00:23:53,807
[Device beeps]

617
00:23:53,891 --> 00:23:58,270
Temp is 100.2,
and heart rate is 96.

618
00:23:58,354 --> 00:24:00,689
Okay, down
from 101.5 and 120.

619
00:24:00,773 --> 00:24:02,232
Very good.

620
00:24:02,316 --> 00:24:04,568
You were out in the heat
in that costume?

621
00:24:04,652 --> 00:24:07,529
Yeah, with about 18,000
of my friends.

622
00:24:07,613 --> 00:24:09,823
- Were you at Anthrocon?
- Uh-huh.

623
00:24:09,907 --> 00:24:11,199
What's that?

624
00:24:11,283 --> 00:24:13,243
Pittsburgh's annual
furry convention.

625
00:24:13,327 --> 00:24:14,828
I go every year.

626
00:24:14,912 --> 00:24:16,496
Ever been?

627
00:24:16,580 --> 00:24:19,332
- Uh, it's not really my scene.
- Mm.

628
00:24:19,416 --> 00:24:20,816
Yeah, furries get a bad rap,

629
00:24:20,834 --> 00:24:23,712
but there are great people
in the community--

630
00:24:23,796 --> 00:24:27,215
Creative, welcoming, funny.

631
00:24:27,299 --> 00:24:30,010
I actually met my girlfriend
at last year's convention.

632
00:24:30,094 --> 00:24:31,636
Oh, that's cute.

633
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:34,472
She gave me hope after
struggling on the dating apps.

634
00:24:34,556 --> 00:24:35,724
Nice to hear

635
00:24:35,808 --> 00:24:38,184
that meeting people
in real life still works.

636
00:24:38,268 --> 00:24:40,979
Wouldn't recommend it,
especially at work.

637
00:24:41,063 --> 00:24:44,024
You should come
to Anthrocon this weekend.

638
00:24:44,108 --> 00:24:46,484
Doesn't she need
a fur suit for that?

639
00:24:46,568 --> 00:24:49,113
I think you'd make
a good dragon.

640
00:24:52,408 --> 00:24:53,700
I'm in.

641
00:24:53,784 --> 00:24:54,993
Balloon up.

642
00:24:55,077 --> 00:24:57,704
[Rapid beeping continues]
Yep, bag her.

643
00:24:57,788 --> 00:24:59,331
Okay.

644
00:24:59,415 --> 00:25:02,208
That was harder without video.
- We won't always have video.

645
00:25:02,292 --> 00:25:03,376
A-fib now at 152.

646
00:25:03,460 --> 00:25:05,253
Blood pressure's
down to 76 over 44.

647
00:25:05,337 --> 00:25:09,424
- Okay, Javadi, sync mode.
Javadi, sync mode, 200, please.

648
00:25:09,508 --> 00:25:11,384
Good end tidal waveform.

649
00:25:11,468 --> 00:25:13,720
Good breath sounds
bilaterally.

650
00:25:13,804 --> 00:25:16,264
[Machine whirs]
- Charged for cardioversion.

651
00:25:16,348 --> 00:25:18,808
Everyone, clear.

652
00:25:18,892 --> 00:25:20,977
[Thump, machine beeps]

653
00:25:21,061 --> 00:25:23,897
- Normal sinus.
- Normal radial pulse.

654
00:25:23,981 --> 00:25:25,231
[Exhales sharply]

655
00:25:25,315 --> 00:25:26,983
- Good.
Keep the fluids going.

656
00:25:27,067 --> 00:25:29,570
Let's see what labs
are back on her.

657
00:25:31,405 --> 00:25:32,447
Nice.

658
00:25:32,531 --> 00:25:35,116
- [Sighs]
- Very nice.

659
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:38,203
- What did you order?
- Um, CBC, ER chem panel.

660
00:25:38,287 --> 00:25:40,789
- Something should be back.
- Fax machine ran out of toner.

661
00:25:40,873 --> 00:25:43,416
Check the chart.
- There is no chart in slot 22.

662
00:25:43,500 --> 00:25:45,919
Check the orders rack.

663
00:25:46,003 --> 00:25:47,462
Nothing here either.

664
00:25:47,546 --> 00:25:50,007
Where's the chart
for Claire Burns?

665
00:25:51,884 --> 00:25:53,259
Claire Burns, order slip.

666
00:25:53,343 --> 00:25:54,928
Never drawn,
never sent off to the lab.

667
00:25:55,012 --> 00:25:56,638
That's cause the patient
wasn't on the board.

668
00:25:56,722 --> 00:25:58,223
Nurses are working zones.

669
00:25:58,307 --> 00:25:59,975
If the patient's not
on the board, they don't exist.

670
00:26:00,059 --> 00:26:01,659
So they didn't shoot
her X-ray?

671
00:26:01,685 --> 00:26:03,937
- X-ray downtime box is empty.
That means it was done.

672
00:26:04,021 --> 00:26:05,647
Then it's
on the portable machine.

673
00:26:05,731 --> 00:26:07,941
Last I saw,
it was headed north.

674
00:26:08,025 --> 00:26:09,818
- Thanks, Dana.
- Yep.

675
00:26:09,902 --> 00:26:11,695
Hey, Kenny,
can you wait up a sec?

676
00:26:11,779 --> 00:26:13,154
If you need an X-ray,
write the order.

677
00:26:13,238 --> 00:26:14,364
Fill out a downtime.

678
00:26:14,448 --> 00:26:16,116
Did you shoot a KUB
in South 22?

679
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:17,450
- No.
Maybe another tech did?

680
00:26:17,534 --> 00:26:19,119
Okay, can you flick
through the films,

681
00:26:19,203 --> 00:26:21,205
look for a patient--
- Burns?

682
00:26:24,583 --> 00:26:25,750
Oh, shit.

683
00:26:25,834 --> 00:26:27,627
Oh, that is a classic
sigmoid volvulus.

684
00:26:27,711 --> 00:26:29,661
- Peritoneal signs.
- Okay, call the OR.

685
00:26:29,713 --> 00:26:32,549
She's going to need
surgery ASAP.

686
00:26:39,723 --> 00:26:41,766
Urine shows three plus blood.

687
00:26:41,850 --> 00:26:43,643
No surprise.

688
00:26:43,727 --> 00:26:45,687
BUN and creatinine
are normal.

689
00:26:45,771 --> 00:26:47,355
No evidence
of renal insufficiency.

690
00:26:47,439 --> 00:26:49,149
I got a good look
at the left kidney--

691
00:26:49,233 --> 00:26:52,318
Mild hydronephrosis consistent
with ureteral column.

692
00:26:52,402 --> 00:26:54,612
How was the rest
of the ultrasound?

693
00:26:54,696 --> 00:26:57,949
Normal. Uh, Pain improved
after 15 ketorolac IM.

694
00:26:58,033 --> 00:27:00,660
Now you can give
another 15 and observe.

695
00:27:00,744 --> 00:27:03,288
Hmm.

696
00:27:03,372 --> 00:27:06,083
Just need you
to cosign my order.

697
00:27:07,918 --> 00:27:09,002
Thank you.

698
00:27:09,086 --> 00:27:11,713
- [Sighs]
- Something on your mind?

699
00:27:11,797 --> 00:27:14,340
Yeah, I-I saw this regular
an hour ago.

700
00:27:14,424 --> 00:27:16,092
He's in his 60s,
fakes an ailment

701
00:27:16,176 --> 00:27:18,553
so he can come in to chat
every now and then

702
00:27:18,637 --> 00:27:20,263
because he's really lonely.

703
00:27:20,347 --> 00:27:22,432
You sure he just doesn't have
a crush on you?

704
00:27:22,516 --> 00:27:25,226
Maybe, but it got me thinking
about my mom.

705
00:27:25,310 --> 00:27:27,937
She's probably
just been lonely.

706
00:27:28,021 --> 00:27:30,106
Yeah.

707
00:27:30,190 --> 00:27:31,566
You know, I, uh...

708
00:27:31,650 --> 00:27:34,235
I haven't really dated
since my divorce.

709
00:27:34,319 --> 00:27:36,571
Medical school,
my kid, residency.

710
00:27:36,655 --> 00:27:39,199
And now I'm feeling
finally kind of ready.

711
00:27:39,283 --> 00:27:41,201
I was waiting
until I got back to Jersey

712
00:27:41,285 --> 00:27:43,036
to work on finding
a relationship,

713
00:27:43,120 --> 00:27:44,620
and now that's out the window.

714
00:27:44,663 --> 00:27:46,748
Maybe I waited too long.

715
00:27:46,832 --> 00:27:47,916
For what?

716
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:49,709
Do you hear that?

717
00:27:49,793 --> 00:27:54,047
That painful, lonely silence
is the sound of my eggs dying.

718
00:27:54,131 --> 00:27:56,841
[Chuckles]

719
00:27:56,925 --> 00:27:58,176
[bell dings]
- Ah.

720
00:27:58,260 --> 00:28:00,220
So the rash in North three
has been discharged.

721
00:28:00,304 --> 00:28:02,104
The Tasered law student
in Central ten

722
00:28:02,181 --> 00:28:03,389
has gone up to psych.

723
00:28:03,473 --> 00:28:05,183
The eye stroke is
now in the ICU.

724
00:28:05,267 --> 00:28:06,893
And the tongue laceration
in South 15

725
00:28:06,977 --> 00:28:08,520
is sobering up
before we discharge,

726
00:28:08,604 --> 00:28:10,396
which better be soon
because we need the room.

727
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:11,606
Okay, I'll grab a med student

728
00:28:11,690 --> 00:28:13,108
and get more patients
moving out.

729
00:28:13,192 --> 00:28:15,142
You're not fazed
by any of this chaos?

730
00:28:15,152 --> 00:28:17,070
- Hmm.
- What a fucking mess.

731
00:28:17,154 --> 00:28:20,073
Jesus Christ, we need you.

732
00:28:20,157 --> 00:28:23,576
Monica Peters, this is our new
attending, Dr. Al-Hashimi.

733
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:25,328
- Welcome.
- Thank you.

734
00:28:25,412 --> 00:28:27,413
Monica's a retired clerk,
best of the best.

735
00:28:27,497 --> 00:28:29,415
She was kind enough
to come in on a holiday

736
00:28:29,499 --> 00:28:31,049
and help get us
back into shape.

737
00:28:31,084 --> 00:28:32,884
Laid off
by the digital revolution,

738
00:28:32,920 --> 00:28:34,462
not retired.
- Okay.

739
00:28:34,546 --> 00:28:37,090
And how's all this digital
shit working out for you now?

740
00:28:37,174 --> 00:28:39,300
- Not so good.
- Exactly.

741
00:28:39,384 --> 00:28:41,177
All right, then,
who's handling

742
00:28:41,261 --> 00:28:43,638
the charts and the orders?
- That's us, right here.

743
00:28:43,722 --> 00:28:45,431
How long have
you been clerks?

744
00:28:45,515 --> 00:28:47,892
- Uh, just today.
We're medical assistants.

745
00:28:47,976 --> 00:28:49,276
Then get out of my space

746
00:28:49,311 --> 00:28:51,479
and go do something
you know how to do.

747
00:28:51,563 --> 00:28:52,814
And no personal calls.

748
00:28:52,898 --> 00:28:54,774
Red phones are
for emergencies only.

749
00:28:54,858 --> 00:28:56,609
This is a hospital,
for God's sake.

750
00:28:56,693 --> 00:28:57,652
I'll call you back.

751
00:28:57,736 --> 00:28:58,987
- Got a gumband?
- Yeah.

752
00:28:59,071 --> 00:29:00,780
Hi. I'm Makedah
from admin and records.

753
00:29:00,864 --> 00:29:02,824
I have a new badge
for a Dr. Whitaker.

754
00:29:02,908 --> 00:29:04,909
- Yeah.
I'll get that to him.

755
00:29:04,993 --> 00:29:06,693
Heard you all
need extra runners?

756
00:29:06,745 --> 00:29:08,621
- Perfect timing.
- How fast can you move?

757
00:29:08,705 --> 00:29:10,290
- I run marathons.
- Great.

758
00:29:10,374 --> 00:29:13,168
Grab the blood samples and the
bin and get them up to the lab.

759
00:29:13,252 --> 00:29:15,628
I want a lab run
every 15 minutes.

760
00:29:15,712 --> 00:29:17,130
Got it.

761
00:29:17,214 --> 00:29:20,384
[Indistinct chatter]

762
00:29:22,386 --> 00:29:24,387
I work at a shoe store
in Oakland.

763
00:29:24,471 --> 00:29:26,389
Full-time
and you're in school?

764
00:29:26,473 --> 00:29:27,974
Yes, and, yes.

765
00:29:28,058 --> 00:29:29,642
Allegheny Community.

766
00:29:29,726 --> 00:29:31,978
Does Jude go
to summer school or camp

767
00:29:32,062 --> 00:29:35,982
while you're
at, uh, work or school?

768
00:29:36,066 --> 00:29:37,984
Can't afford it.

769
00:29:38,068 --> 00:29:39,569
Are there any other
family members

770
00:29:39,653 --> 00:29:41,988
that could help with his care
when you're not available?

771
00:29:42,072 --> 00:29:43,407
No.

772
00:29:46,576 --> 00:29:47,827
Chantal, we want to help you,

773
00:29:47,911 --> 00:29:50,455
but we can't help
if you won't talk to us.

774
00:29:50,539 --> 00:29:52,540
What, you're
gonna take Jude away

775
00:29:52,624 --> 00:29:54,334
and put him in foster care?

776
00:29:54,418 --> 00:29:57,378
I promised my parents
that would never happen.

777
00:29:57,462 --> 00:29:59,714
Did your parents pass away?

778
00:29:59,798 --> 00:30:01,174
Nope.

779
00:30:01,258 --> 00:30:04,803
- What happened to them?
- [Sighs]

780
00:30:09,308 --> 00:30:12,644
My parents were deported
to Haiti nine months ago.

781
00:30:12,728 --> 00:30:15,188
[Breathes shakily]

782
00:30:15,272 --> 00:30:18,233
They went in for their
immigration hearing and were...

783
00:30:18,317 --> 00:30:20,526
Detained.

784
00:30:20,610 --> 00:30:22,445
I was a sophomore at Ithaca.

785
00:30:22,529 --> 00:30:26,115
I had to move back home
to take care of my brother.

786
00:30:26,199 --> 00:30:27,784
I'm sorry.

787
00:30:27,868 --> 00:30:32,413
It was either that, or he
moved back to Haiti with them.

788
00:30:32,497 --> 00:30:34,958
He's never been there.

789
00:30:35,042 --> 00:30:37,461
We were both born here.

790
00:30:39,129 --> 00:30:43,424
[Scoffs] My mom was so excited
when I got into college.

791
00:30:43,508 --> 00:30:45,551
She worked so hard

792
00:30:45,635 --> 00:30:48,554
to save up and pay my tuition.

793
00:30:48,638 --> 00:30:50,556
And now all she wants

794
00:30:50,640 --> 00:30:53,060
is for my brother
to finish high school.

795
00:30:54,978 --> 00:30:57,021
Man, being a big sister's
a lot easier

796
00:30:57,105 --> 00:30:59,066
than being a surrogate mom.

797
00:31:01,651 --> 00:31:03,361
Just give us a moment,
please,

798
00:31:03,445 --> 00:31:05,906
and I'll come grab you
when we're done.

799
00:31:09,368 --> 00:31:11,918
Do we really need to get
family services involved?

800
00:31:11,953 --> 00:31:13,913
You wanted to get
them involved this morning

801
00:31:13,997 --> 00:31:16,124
with your eight-year-old
ITP patient.

802
00:31:16,208 --> 00:31:18,751
- That's different.
Abuse trumps neglect.

803
00:31:18,835 --> 00:31:20,735
We can't separate her
from her brother.

804
00:31:20,754 --> 00:31:22,255
It's not right.

805
00:31:22,339 --> 00:31:25,189
A lot of what happens to
people around here isn't right.

806
00:31:27,928 --> 00:31:29,679
[Person groaning]

807
00:31:29,763 --> 00:31:32,765
McKay, patient's
complaining of pain.

808
00:31:32,849 --> 00:31:35,601
Uh, yeah.

809
00:31:35,685 --> 00:31:38,354
Hey, Amaya.
What's going on?

810
00:31:38,438 --> 00:31:40,188
Oh, it really
fucking hurts again.

811
00:31:40,232 --> 00:31:42,150
Hey, Jesse,
can you grab Whitaker?

812
00:31:42,234 --> 00:31:44,694
When did it get bad?
- Two minutes ago. Aah!

813
00:31:44,778 --> 00:31:46,779
Giving you some morphine
to take the edge off.

814
00:31:46,863 --> 00:31:50,283
How severe, one to ten?
- Ah. 12. It's way worse.

815
00:31:50,367 --> 00:31:51,617
Okay.

816
00:31:51,701 --> 00:31:53,619
Hey, Amaya, the meds
will kick in,

817
00:31:53,703 --> 00:31:55,603
and we'll get you back
on the foot rest

818
00:31:55,664 --> 00:31:58,750
to see what's going on, okay?
- [Groaning]

819
00:31:58,834 --> 00:32:01,461
[door opens, closes]

820
00:32:01,545 --> 00:32:04,964
I had to call her husband
in New York to get consent.

821
00:32:05,048 --> 00:32:06,007
Okay.

822
00:32:06,091 --> 00:32:08,468
Dr. Shamsi
will be operating.

823
00:32:08,552 --> 00:32:10,470
If she presented
with peritoneal signs,

824
00:32:10,554 --> 00:32:12,096
why wasn't I called?

825
00:32:12,180 --> 00:32:14,807
There was
a delayed presentation.

826
00:32:14,891 --> 00:32:16,491
The X-ray was shot
an hour ago.

827
00:32:16,560 --> 00:32:18,019
Why didn't anybody read it?

828
00:32:18,103 --> 00:32:19,979
There was confusion
with the digital systems down.

829
00:32:20,063 --> 00:32:21,647
It wasn't read.
We didn't get a report.

830
00:32:21,731 --> 00:32:24,359
An hour ago, I could have
fixed this in 60 seconds

831
00:32:24,443 --> 00:32:25,985
with a rectal tube.

832
00:32:26,069 --> 00:32:27,653
Now she needs major surgery.

833
00:32:27,737 --> 00:32:30,531
- I'm sorry.
- Not good enough, nepo baby.

834
00:32:30,615 --> 00:32:32,116
You fucked up.

835
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:34,660
Don't trust anything or anybody
else when the system's down.

836
00:32:34,744 --> 00:32:36,162
[Elevator bell dings]

837
00:32:36,246 --> 00:32:39,749
With all the chaos, she
just fell through the cracks.

838
00:32:41,334 --> 00:32:44,087
She almost died.

839
00:32:44,171 --> 00:32:45,838
I could have killed her.

840
00:32:45,922 --> 00:32:47,673
- Whitaker.
- No--

841
00:32:47,757 --> 00:32:50,176
McKay needs you
in Central 11.

842
00:32:50,260 --> 00:32:51,844
We caught it in time.

843
00:32:51,928 --> 00:32:54,431
We won't let it
happen again, okay?

844
00:33:05,775 --> 00:33:08,236
Oh, uh, Princess
is looking for you.

845
00:33:08,320 --> 00:33:11,406
Um, she said something
about Monica under her breath,

846
00:33:11,490 --> 00:33:14,867
but I couldn't make it out.
- Okay, I'll be back in a sec.

847
00:33:14,951 --> 00:33:17,703
Hey. Hey.

848
00:33:17,787 --> 00:33:21,416
You did good with that
sexual-assault victim.

849
00:33:21,500 --> 00:33:23,543
You were amazing with her.

850
00:33:23,627 --> 00:33:25,628
We do what we can to provide
the best care

851
00:33:25,712 --> 00:33:29,048
to traumatized people
in their darkest days.

852
00:33:29,132 --> 00:33:30,532
What'd you talk to her about

853
00:33:30,550 --> 00:33:32,468
when you took her out
on the walk?

854
00:33:32,552 --> 00:33:34,637
I, um...

855
00:33:34,721 --> 00:33:36,639
Told her there might be a time
in the future

856
00:33:36,723 --> 00:33:41,561
when she changes her mind,
wants to press charges.

857
00:33:41,645 --> 00:33:44,439
It's better to have
the option to do it than not.

858
00:33:44,523 --> 00:33:46,816
Smart.

859
00:33:48,860 --> 00:33:50,403
Is every day like this?

860
00:33:50,487 --> 00:33:54,574
Minus the cyberattacks, yeah.

861
00:33:54,658 --> 00:33:56,576
But you're only
a few hours away

862
00:33:56,660 --> 00:33:59,245
from being done
with your first of many.

863
00:33:59,329 --> 00:34:00,621
Be proud of that.

864
00:34:00,705 --> 00:34:03,917
[Distant train horn blowing]

865
00:34:07,671 --> 00:34:09,714
You're gonna want to be
on a soft diet,

866
00:34:09,798 --> 00:34:12,800
so, uh, things
like, uh, mashed potatoes,

867
00:34:12,884 --> 00:34:14,886
soup, mac and cheese are good.

868
00:34:14,970 --> 00:34:16,429
I was gonna make

869
00:34:16,513 --> 00:34:18,313
your favorite
three-bean dip tonight.

870
00:34:18,390 --> 00:34:20,266
- [Lisping]
Bitch, that is so nice.

871
00:34:20,350 --> 00:34:21,642
See, I am nice.

872
00:34:21,726 --> 00:34:23,394
Could she have that?

873
00:34:23,478 --> 00:34:26,355
Uh, yeah. Yeah, yeah,
if you eat it with a spoon

874
00:34:26,439 --> 00:34:28,139
rather than anything,
like, crunchy

875
00:34:28,191 --> 00:34:30,341
that could work its way
into the laceration.

876
00:34:30,360 --> 00:34:31,277
Both:
Mm.

877
00:34:31,361 --> 00:34:33,029
So she'll need
to be spoon-fed?

878
00:34:33,113 --> 00:34:34,322
[Chuckles]

879
00:34:34,406 --> 00:34:36,324
Antibiotics
three times a day.

880
00:34:36,408 --> 00:34:38,451
Come back here in two days
for a wound check.

881
00:34:38,535 --> 00:34:41,662
See you then, Doctor.

882
00:34:41,746 --> 00:34:45,500
Checking blood flow
to the ovary.

883
00:34:49,671 --> 00:34:52,465
- Something wrong?
- Intermittent torsion.

884
00:34:52,549 --> 00:34:54,133
What's that?

885
00:34:54,217 --> 00:34:56,636
I'm coming out now.

886
00:34:56,720 --> 00:34:58,804
We will slide you back.
Thanks.

887
00:34:58,888 --> 00:35:02,433
- [Sighs deeply]
- Your ovary is twisting

888
00:35:02,517 --> 00:35:04,143
and cutting off
the blood supply.

889
00:35:04,227 --> 00:35:06,145
That's what's been causing
your pain.

890
00:35:06,229 --> 00:35:09,690
Ah. You said the blood supply
was fine before.

891
00:35:09,774 --> 00:35:13,277
Sometimes the ovary
can twist randomly.

892
00:35:13,361 --> 00:35:16,822
In those cases,
the pain can come and go.

893
00:35:16,906 --> 00:35:19,951
- Can you fix it?
- With surgery.

894
00:35:20,035 --> 00:35:21,202
"Surgery"?

895
00:35:21,286 --> 00:35:23,037
The ovary needs
to be untwisted

896
00:35:23,121 --> 00:35:26,040
and tacked down with a stitch
so this doesn't happen again.

897
00:35:26,124 --> 00:35:29,502
If we can get you upstairs
quickly, we can save it.

898
00:35:29,586 --> 00:35:32,004
I could lose my ovary?

899
00:35:32,088 --> 00:35:33,923
Will I still be able
to have a baby?

900
00:35:34,007 --> 00:35:36,175
This shouldn't be
an issue in the future.

901
00:35:36,259 --> 00:35:37,843
Dr. McKay made the right call

902
00:35:37,927 --> 00:35:39,929
to keep you in the ER
for observation

903
00:35:40,013 --> 00:35:43,724
so we could catch it
if the pain returned.

904
00:35:43,808 --> 00:35:45,226
Thank you.

905
00:35:45,310 --> 00:35:48,104
- I'll call GYN.
- Yeah.

906
00:35:48,188 --> 00:35:49,855
[Bell dings]

907
00:35:49,939 --> 00:35:51,857
- Hey, welcome back.
How was the trip?

908
00:35:51,941 --> 00:35:53,901
- Smooth sailing.
Presby's pretty nice.

909
00:35:53,985 --> 00:35:56,612
I might have to pick up
some day shifts over there.

910
00:35:56,696 --> 00:35:58,698
<i>- [Electronic voice]
Dr. Abbot's funny.</i>

911
00:35:58,782 --> 00:36:00,658
Trust me,
his charm wears off.

912
00:36:00,742 --> 00:36:02,243
- No, it doesn't.
- He's not sedated?

913
00:36:02,327 --> 00:36:04,537
I gave him Versed for
the CT scan on the ride back,

914
00:36:04,621 --> 00:36:06,539
but I figured he'd need to be
awake and alert

915
00:36:06,623 --> 00:36:07,832
to give consent.
- "Consent"?

916
00:36:07,916 --> 00:36:09,417
- Yep.
We're going to get you settled.

917
00:36:09,501 --> 00:36:11,502
Why don't you page Garcia
to come down?

918
00:36:11,586 --> 00:36:13,254
- Dr. Robby.
- You got this?

919
00:36:13,338 --> 00:36:15,423
- You know I got it.
- Yep.

920
00:36:15,507 --> 00:36:17,508
All right, Howard.

921
00:36:17,592 --> 00:36:19,677
Hey, I want to debrief
with you later

922
00:36:19,761 --> 00:36:21,095
on your sigmoid volvulus
patient.

923
00:36:21,179 --> 00:36:22,888
I finished with your
fireworks kid's sister.

924
00:36:22,972 --> 00:36:24,322
- And?
- She's a responsible

925
00:36:24,349 --> 00:36:25,933
young woman
and a good guardian to Jude.

926
00:36:26,017 --> 00:36:28,185
There is no reason to get
family services involved today.

927
00:36:28,269 --> 00:36:29,562
That's good.

928
00:36:29,646 --> 00:36:31,230
Because he's
in the hospital for surgery,

929
00:36:31,314 --> 00:36:33,232
but they will most likely make
a home visit next week

930
00:36:33,316 --> 00:36:34,900
to evaluate the safety
of their apartment

931
00:36:34,984 --> 00:36:36,444
and the care
that Chantal can provide,

932
00:36:36,528 --> 00:36:38,070
along with her
other responsibilities.

933
00:36:38,154 --> 00:36:39,780
- And then what?
They take Jude?

934
00:36:39,864 --> 00:36:42,074
In my experience, they'll
make the same assessment I did.

935
00:36:42,158 --> 00:36:43,784
They don't like
to separate siblings.

936
00:36:43,868 --> 00:36:45,578
Anything else
we can do for 'em?

937
00:36:45,662 --> 00:36:47,496
I'll get some resources
together for Chantal--

938
00:36:47,580 --> 00:36:49,081
Summer after-school programs.

939
00:36:49,165 --> 00:36:51,083
But there might come a point
when he'd be better off

940
00:36:51,167 --> 00:36:52,335
with his parents in Haiti.

941
00:36:52,419 --> 00:36:53,794
His parents want him
to stay here.

942
00:36:53,878 --> 00:36:55,296
It's what's best
for the child.

943
00:36:55,380 --> 00:36:56,922
- Says who?
- Dr. Santos.

944
00:36:57,006 --> 00:36:58,258
Come on.

945
00:37:00,051 --> 00:37:02,219
- Welcome back, Mr. Knox.
What did we discover?

946
00:37:02,303 --> 00:37:04,953
Diverticular abscess
that progressed to perforation,

947
00:37:05,014 --> 00:37:06,766
now with free air
under the diaphragm.

948
00:37:06,850 --> 00:37:08,601
<i>- [Electronic voice]
In English, please?</i>

949
00:37:08,685 --> 00:37:10,269
There's a small hole
in the colon

950
00:37:10,353 --> 00:37:11,979
that's spilling bacteria
into the abdomen.

951
00:37:12,063 --> 00:37:15,941
You're likely to develop
peritonitis and sepsis.

952
00:37:16,025 --> 00:37:17,610
<i>- [Electronic voice]
How bad?</i>

953
00:37:17,694 --> 00:37:19,070
You need surgery now.

954
00:37:19,154 --> 00:37:22,782
You have a 100% chance
of death without it.

955
00:37:22,866 --> 00:37:24,451
<i>- [Electronic voice]
With it?</i>

956
00:37:26,661 --> 00:37:28,705
50% chance.

957
00:37:31,332 --> 00:37:32,792
<i>- [Electronic voice]
I could die?</i>

958
00:37:32,876 --> 00:37:34,919
Yes, but we're very good
at what we do.

959
00:37:35,003 --> 00:37:37,880
That is what
the consent is for.

960
00:37:37,964 --> 00:37:39,799
<i>- [Electronic voice]
What about my sister?</i>

961
00:37:39,883 --> 00:37:42,343
- We found her.
She'd like to speak with you.

962
00:37:42,427 --> 00:37:44,011
We don't have time for that.

963
00:37:44,095 --> 00:37:46,514
Any delay increases
your mortality risks.

964
00:37:46,598 --> 00:37:49,684
<i>[Electronic voice] I want
to talk to my sister first.</i>

965
00:37:52,979 --> 00:37:55,731
We're gonna make
that happen for you.

966
00:37:55,815 --> 00:37:59,068
I'll have them prep an OR,
but make it fast, very fast.

967
00:37:59,152 --> 00:38:02,238
Yeah. We're on the move
again, Howard.

968
00:38:02,322 --> 00:38:05,492
[Indistinct chatter]

969
00:38:16,753 --> 00:38:18,505
Hey.

970
00:38:20,423 --> 00:38:22,801
The ice cream party over?

971
00:38:24,594 --> 00:38:26,679
Yes.

972
00:38:26,763 --> 00:38:29,890
Do you need anything?

973
00:38:29,974 --> 00:38:31,684
[Sighs softly]

974
00:38:31,768 --> 00:38:33,812
A time machine.

975
00:38:37,690 --> 00:38:39,943
That'd be nice,
wouldn't it?

976
00:38:44,280 --> 00:38:47,366
I don't even know
what hurts more--

977
00:38:47,450 --> 00:38:50,537
The cancer or...

978
00:38:52,664 --> 00:38:56,167
Knowing I'm never gonna see
my sons grow up.

979
00:38:58,545 --> 00:39:00,964
It feels like a cruel joke.

980
00:39:02,465 --> 00:39:07,052
Why give me children
and a husband I adore

981
00:39:07,136 --> 00:39:10,890
if you're just gonna
take them away from me?

982
00:39:10,974 --> 00:39:14,351
For what?
Fucking lung cancer.

983
00:39:14,435 --> 00:39:17,521
[Breathes deeply]

984
00:39:17,605 --> 00:39:19,523
I didn't even smoke.

985
00:39:19,607 --> 00:39:22,819
[Breathing heavily]

986
00:39:27,532 --> 00:39:29,659
Do you believe in God?

987
00:39:31,953 --> 00:39:34,163
I like the concept.

988
00:39:38,042 --> 00:39:41,337
I'm sure you've seen
a lot of death.

989
00:39:41,421 --> 00:39:43,423
I have seen my share.

990
00:39:46,175 --> 00:39:48,219
Any advice?

991
00:39:53,850 --> 00:39:56,603
I've never died before.

992
00:40:05,904 --> 00:40:07,613
- Hey, sorry.
W-we're outside.

993
00:40:07,697 --> 00:40:11,158
There's, um--there's no
cell service inside right now,

994
00:40:11,242 --> 00:40:12,744
but, um, here he is.

995
00:40:14,996 --> 00:40:16,413
<i>Oh, my God.</i>

996
00:40:16,497 --> 00:40:18,791
<i>Are you all right?</i>

997
00:40:20,043 --> 00:40:21,752
<i>- [Electronic voice]
Been better.</i>

998
00:40:21,836 --> 00:40:24,129
<i>You look beautiful.</i>

999
00:40:24,213 --> 00:40:25,756
<i>Thank you.</i>

1000
00:40:25,840 --> 00:40:28,051
<i>You're not looking so hot.</i>

1001
00:40:30,178 --> 00:40:32,972
<i>- [Electronic voice]
Thank you for calling back.</i>

1002
00:40:35,183 --> 00:40:36,809
<i>Of course.</i>

1003
00:40:36,893 --> 00:40:39,728
<i>I'm sorry
that it's been this long.</i>

1004
00:40:39,812 --> 00:40:43,315
<i>All the stuff with Dad
and the drinking, I--</i>

1005
00:40:43,399 --> 00:40:46,485
<i>I had to do what was best
for me and Tommy.</i>

1006
00:40:46,569 --> 00:40:48,988
<i>- [Electronic voice]
How is Tommy?</i>

1007
00:40:49,072 --> 00:40:52,992
<i>Starting his junior year
in high school next month,</i>

1008
00:40:53,076 --> 00:40:56,454
<i>16 and already has
a girlfriend.</i>

1009
00:40:58,414 --> 00:41:00,666
<i>- [Electronic voice]
Takes after his uncle.</i>

1010
00:41:00,750 --> 00:41:02,710
<i>[Laughs]</i>

1011
00:41:02,794 --> 00:41:04,378
<i>Maybe we can make a plan</i>

1012
00:41:04,462 --> 00:41:07,173
<i>for you to see each other
over the holidays.</i>

1013
00:41:11,386 --> 00:41:13,471
<i>- [Electronic voice]
I'd love that.</i>

1014
00:41:14,931 --> 00:41:16,766
<i>Is the doctor there?</i>

1015
00:41:18,559 --> 00:41:20,019
Hi, I'm Dr. Abbot.

1016
00:41:20,103 --> 00:41:21,812
<i>Can you call me
when he gets out of surgery?</i>

1017
00:41:21,896 --> 00:41:23,981
Of course, but right now we
need to get him up to the OR.

1018
00:41:24,065 --> 00:41:25,566
<i>- I understand.
Thanks.</i>

1019
00:41:25,650 --> 00:41:27,443
<i>Talk to you soon, Howard.</i>

1020
00:41:29,445 --> 00:41:32,907
<i>Oh, I forgot to tell him
I love him.</i>

1021
00:41:32,991 --> 00:41:34,199
Oh, wow.

1022
00:41:34,283 --> 00:41:36,076
Monica?

1023
00:41:36,160 --> 00:41:37,369
Welcome back.

1024
00:41:37,453 --> 00:41:39,413
Robinavitch.

1025
00:41:39,497 --> 00:41:42,207
Two for the lab, three for CT.
- I'll take those.

1026
00:41:42,291 --> 00:41:44,919
They need me upstairs.
- On it for CT.

1027
00:41:45,003 --> 00:41:46,211
You run a tight ship.

1028
00:41:46,295 --> 00:41:48,255
Well, it's
a work in progress.

1029
00:41:48,339 --> 00:41:50,716
- Is he going up?
- Yeah.

1030
00:41:50,800 --> 00:41:53,385
He's a good guy.

1031
00:41:53,469 --> 00:41:56,221
Our surgeons
will get him through.

1032
00:41:56,305 --> 00:42:00,142
[Indistinct chatter, laughter]

1033
00:42:00,226 --> 00:42:02,895
I like her.

1034
00:42:02,979 --> 00:42:04,647
More than me?

1035
00:42:04,731 --> 00:42:07,107
Only time will tell.

1036
00:42:07,191 --> 00:42:08,984
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

1037
00:42:09,068 --> 00:42:11,612
She has good command
of staff and procedures.

1038
00:42:11,696 --> 00:42:14,907
I think you're leaving your day
shift in very capable hands.

1039
00:42:14,991 --> 00:42:16,408
I hope so.

1040
00:42:16,492 --> 00:42:18,369
All right,
I'm out of here, man.

1041
00:42:18,453 --> 00:42:21,455
I got to be back
in a few hours for my shift.

1042
00:42:21,539 --> 00:42:23,290
Well, hey,
if I don't see you...

1043
00:42:23,374 --> 00:42:26,043
You're really doing
this still?

1044
00:42:26,127 --> 00:42:28,087
I don't think I can remember
the last time

1045
00:42:28,171 --> 00:42:29,630
you took three days off
in a row.

1046
00:42:29,714 --> 00:42:32,424
I've taken a vacation before.

1047
00:42:32,508 --> 00:42:34,385
Name the last one.

1048
00:42:34,469 --> 00:42:36,971
[Inhales deeply]

1049
00:42:37,055 --> 00:42:39,390
Point taken.

1050
00:42:39,474 --> 00:42:42,769
It's gonna be a lot of time
to self-reflect.

1051
00:42:45,188 --> 00:42:47,398
You sure you can handle that?

1052
00:42:49,692 --> 00:42:51,443
Okay.

1053
00:42:51,527 --> 00:42:53,612
You just make sure
you come back.

1054
00:42:53,696 --> 00:42:56,407
And if it gets dark,
you call me.

1055
00:42:58,034 --> 00:42:59,786
You listening?

1056
00:43:04,248 --> 00:43:06,458
So the ankle's negative
for fracture.

1057
00:43:06,542 --> 00:43:08,627
Wait, go back to the ankle.

1058
00:43:08,711 --> 00:43:10,170
You see the normal mortise?

1059
00:43:10,254 --> 00:43:13,298
Yeah, but the tibiofibular
clear space looks enlarged,

1060
00:43:13,382 --> 00:43:16,468
and the tibiofibular overlap
seems reduced.

1061
00:43:16,552 --> 00:43:19,847
Maybe a little.

1062
00:43:19,931 --> 00:43:22,933
Eight millimeters, three millimeters.

1063
00:43:23,017 --> 00:43:25,352
Seems like a tear
in the syndesmotic ligaments.

1064
00:43:25,436 --> 00:43:27,479
Doesn't that need
surgical fixation?

1065
00:43:27,563 --> 00:43:30,441
- They do.
I can request an MRI.

1066
00:43:30,525 --> 00:43:33,652
Um, have you done
a radiology clerkship before?

1067
00:43:33,736 --> 00:43:36,656
No, I'm just that good.

1068
00:43:38,407 --> 00:43:42,036
- [Chuckles]
- I'm good at things, too.

1069
00:43:42,120 --> 00:43:43,663
[Chuckles]

1070
00:43:52,130 --> 00:43:57,051
Really great work
earlier today, Doctor.

1071
00:43:57,135 --> 00:43:59,720
Huh.

1072
00:43:59,804 --> 00:44:01,055
Ow, wow.

1073
00:44:01,139 --> 00:44:03,515
You can just call me Whitaker.
- Not a chance.

1074
00:44:03,599 --> 00:44:04,767
You earned that.

1075
00:44:04,851 --> 00:44:06,185
I'm proud of you.

1076
00:44:06,269 --> 00:44:07,895
We all are.

1077
00:44:07,979 --> 00:44:09,146
Thank you.

1078
00:44:09,230 --> 00:44:11,607
- Busy day.
- Oh, yeah.

1079
00:44:11,691 --> 00:44:14,401
So you're
a very empathetic soul.

1080
00:44:14,485 --> 00:44:16,695
- Yeah, I'd like to think--
- I'm not finished yet.

1081
00:44:16,779 --> 00:44:19,079
And you want to be there
for all your patients.

1082
00:44:19,157 --> 00:44:20,741
- Don't you?
- Shh.

1083
00:44:20,825 --> 00:44:22,034
Sorry.

1084
00:44:22,118 --> 00:44:24,328
So this relationship
that you're having

1085
00:44:24,412 --> 00:44:26,830
with this woman, um,
the widow of the burn victim

1086
00:44:26,914 --> 00:44:28,665
who died last year.
- Amy.

1087
00:44:28,749 --> 00:44:30,042
Santos tell you?

1088
00:44:30,126 --> 00:44:32,503
I understand
you're helping her out.

1089
00:44:32,587 --> 00:44:34,338
Yeah, on the farm.

1090
00:44:34,422 --> 00:44:37,216
I grew up on one, and Amy's--

1091
00:44:37,300 --> 00:44:39,843
Mrs. Miller is getting
pressure to sell,

1092
00:44:39,927 --> 00:44:42,012
so I'm just helping out.

1093
00:44:42,096 --> 00:44:44,056
What about her friends
and family?

1094
00:44:44,140 --> 00:44:45,891
Yeah, they're around.

1095
00:44:45,975 --> 00:44:47,392
Supporting her?

1096
00:44:47,476 --> 00:44:48,977
Yeah, I think they try to,

1097
00:44:49,061 --> 00:44:52,397
but, mostly,
she's just leaning on...

1098
00:44:52,481 --> 00:44:53,900
Me.

1099
00:44:56,819 --> 00:44:58,737
I'm sure
she's really grateful

1100
00:44:58,821 --> 00:45:00,171
for everything that you do,

1101
00:45:00,239 --> 00:45:03,117
but it's important
to have boundaries.

1102
00:45:03,201 --> 00:45:04,535
Yeah.

1103
00:45:07,705 --> 00:45:10,749
Hey, you want to do me
a favor?

1104
00:45:10,833 --> 00:45:12,084
Yeah?

1105
00:45:12,168 --> 00:45:14,920
You want to house-sit for me
while I'm gone?

1106
00:45:15,004 --> 00:45:16,922
You'd actually be
helping me out,

1107
00:45:17,006 --> 00:45:20,259
and you could save
some money on rent.

1108
00:45:20,343 --> 00:45:21,760
Are you being serious?

1109
00:45:21,844 --> 00:45:24,805
No smoking, no parties,
no pets, no babies,

1110
00:45:24,889 --> 00:45:26,598
yours or anybody else's.

1111
00:45:26,682 --> 00:45:29,268
- I don't have a baby.
- No, but she does.

1112
00:45:29,352 --> 00:45:32,396
I was going to ask Abbot, but
he does nude yoga at sunrise,

1113
00:45:32,480 --> 00:45:34,606
and I don't think some
of my elderly neighbors

1114
00:45:34,690 --> 00:45:36,900
would survive seeing that.
- [Chuckles]

1115
00:45:36,984 --> 00:45:39,945
Yeah.
Yeah, t-that would be amazing--

1116
00:45:40,029 --> 00:45:43,407
The house-sitting,
not seeing Abbot's naked yoga.

1117
00:45:43,491 --> 00:45:46,118
If I don't come back, you got
a swinging bachelor pad.

1118
00:45:46,202 --> 00:45:47,620
Okay.

1119
00:45:48,996 --> 00:45:50,581
Come find me
before you leave.

1120
00:45:50,665 --> 00:45:52,916
I'll give you my keys
and the security code.

1121
00:45:53,000 --> 00:45:54,168
Okay.

1122
00:45:54,252 --> 00:45:57,462
Who's the joker
that did this?

1123
00:45:57,546 --> 00:45:59,548
Oh.

1124
00:45:59,632 --> 00:46:01,133
We need some help out there.

1125
00:46:01,217 --> 00:46:03,302
You two, make sure
to double-check your work.

1126
00:46:03,386 --> 00:46:04,936
Triage could use an extra hand.

1127
00:46:04,971 --> 00:46:06,972
Princess, finish up here,
then head that way.

1128
00:46:07,056 --> 00:46:09,308
- Three for CT now.
Should I run it over?

1129
00:46:09,392 --> 00:46:10,976
- No.
Keep taking off orders.

1130
00:46:11,060 --> 00:46:13,061
CT's gonna get backed up
if we wait on these.

1131
00:46:13,145 --> 00:46:15,189
I know, but I can't waste
a runner on that right now.

1132
00:46:15,273 --> 00:46:17,232
Where'd you find
a carrier sheet?

1133
00:46:17,316 --> 00:46:20,068
Exactly where I filed it away
ten years ago.

1134
00:46:20,152 --> 00:46:22,154
I thought that thing
didn't work.

1135
00:46:22,238 --> 00:46:24,031
Can't receive,
but it can send.

1136
00:46:24,115 --> 00:46:26,909
[Telephone ringing]

1137
00:46:31,205 --> 00:46:34,458
Stay hydrated, preferably
with electrolyte-rich drinks

1138
00:46:34,542 --> 00:46:36,710
like coconut water.
- I'm not a fan of coconuts.

1139
00:46:36,794 --> 00:46:38,337
Okay, Gatorade's
also an option.

1140
00:46:38,421 --> 00:46:40,672
Just avoid alcohol and
caffeine, and I suggest wearing

1141
00:46:40,756 --> 00:46:42,341
light, breathable clothing.
- Boring.

1142
00:46:42,425 --> 00:46:44,301
Come back
if your symptoms worsen,

1143
00:46:44,385 --> 00:46:46,053
if you develop
a headache or confusion.

1144
00:46:46,137 --> 00:46:47,346
Okay.

1145
00:46:47,430 --> 00:46:50,349
Mm.
You sure about that?

1146
00:46:50,433 --> 00:46:52,351
[Indistinct chatter]

1147
00:46:52,435 --> 00:46:55,395
- Hey, could you turn that up?
- [Gasps]

1148
00:46:55,479 --> 00:46:58,732
<i>Have responded to a deadly
waterslide collapse</i>

1149
00:46:58,816 --> 00:47:00,234
<i>at a local water park.</i>

1150
00:47:00,318 --> 00:47:02,402
<i>Now, we're told there's
at least one fatality,</i>

1151
00:47:02,486 --> 00:47:03,737
<i>with multiple injuries.</i>

1152
00:47:03,821 --> 00:47:06,865
- Oh, shit.
And they're all coming to us.

1153
00:47:06,949 --> 00:47:09,869
<i>Currently being airlifted
to the hospital by heli--</i>

